<title>USA: Lexington County, S.C., to hold school bond vote.</title>
<headline>Lexington County, S.C., to hold school bond vote.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBIA, S.C. 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Carolina's Lexington County School District 3 has scheduled a March 8 referendum on a $12.9 million general obligation bond issue, the State newspaper said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The school board unanimously approved the proposal Tuesday night to finance construction of a new middle school and a district auditorium.</p>
<p>School Superintendent Ray Geddings said the issue would be timed to coincide with the expiration of outstanding bonds, in order to keep any tax increase to a minimum.</p>
<p>--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
</text>
